From: Andre Ziviani <andrepziviani@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:38:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: r3k: probe the Lexra RLX5281

The RLX5281 is an R3000-class core: CP0 Status keeps a KU/IE stack,
exceptions return with rfe, EntryHi holds a 6-bit ASID at bit 6. The
board builds it as plain CPU_R3000, so every one of those sites takes
the R3000 branch mainline already has. The one thing missing is the
probe: the core reports PRId 0x0000dc02 (legacy company, implementation
0xdc), which matches neither case here, so cpu_probe() leaves the name
NULL and the BUG_ON after the switch fires before trap_init(). Add the
case. No MIPS_CPU_3K_CACHE: the Lexra caches are not R3000 isolated-cache
caches, and the board installs its own cache code.

---
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-r3k-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-r3k-probe.c
@@ -117,6 +117,12 @@
 			c->options |= MIPS_CPU_FPU;
 		c->tlbsize = 64;
 		break;
+	case PRID_COMP_LEGACY | 0xdc00:	/* Lexra RLX5281 */
+		c->cputype = CPU_R3000;
+		__cpu_name[cpu] = "RLX5281";
+		c->options = MIPS_CPU_TLB | MIPS_CPU_NOFPUEX;
+		c->tlbsize = 64;
+		break;
 	}
 
 	BUG_ON(!__cpu_name[cpu]);
